{number: 96}
{title: Leaning on the Everlasting Arms}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] What a fellowship, what a joy divine,
Leaning on the ever-[G7] lasting arms;
What a [C] blessedness, what a peace is mine,
Leaning on the ever-[G7] lasting [C] arms.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Leaning, [F] leaning,
Safe and secure from [G7] all alarms;
[C] Leaning, [F] leaning,
Leaning on the [G7] everlasting [C] arms.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
O how [C] sweet to walk in this pilgrim way,
Leaning on the ever-[G7] lasting arms;
O how [C] bright the path grows from day to day,
Leaning on the ever-[G7] lasting [C] arms.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
What have [C] I to dread, what have I to fear,
Leaning on the ever-[G7] lasting arms?
I have [C] blessed peace with my Lord so near,
Leaning on the ever-[G7] lasting [C] arms.
{end_of_verse}
